# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Responsive, Reflow & Zoom Standards (Guide #6)

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-RESPONSIVE-REFLOW-ZOOM-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

All UI **MUST** work across breakpoints, reflow, and zoom levels defined in the guide. Read before layout work.

## Non-negotiables

- **Mobile and desktop** share the same authoritative business state — not divergent features.
- Content **reflows** at 320px width — no horizontal scroll for primary tasks.
- **200% zoom** must not break primary workflows.
- Touch targets and spacing adapt per breakpoint rules in the full doc.
- Tables on narrow viewports: responsive pattern from Guide #7 — not clipped overflow.
- Sidebars collapse predictably; primary actions remain reachable.
- Do not hide critical actions only on mobile without equivalent access.

## Verification

Test narrow viewport and zoom before declaring responsive work complete.
